{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01XojzaPGPSaZ5Py5UGS2hLD", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_13\"}, {\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_12\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo13\"}, {\"url\": \"https://apolloexplorer.co.uk/books/sp-4214/app5.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://irc.astro.univie.ac.at/kiwix/content/wikipedia_en_100_2023-11/A/Apollo_13\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.slideshare.net/slideshow/apollo-11-115193652/115193652\"}, {\"url\": \"https://orbitcodex.com/operations/apollo-13-saturn-v\"}, {\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.com/wiki/Apollo_12\"}, {\"url\": \"https://he.wikipedia.org@en.wikipedia.com/wiki/Apollo_12\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T12:59:32.078Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Apollo 11 Apollo 12 Apollo 13 launch mass kg", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01722wgwdx8cvgG9PfbB1pZf", "content": [{"title": "Apollo 13", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_13"}, {"title": "Apollo 12", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_12"}, {"title": "www.wikipedia.org", "url": "https://www.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo13"}, {"title": "Where No Man Has Gone Before: A History of Apollo Lunar Exploration Missions", "url": "https://apolloexplorer.co.uk/books/sp-4214/app5.html"}, {"title": "Apollo 13", "url": "https://irc.astro.univie.ac.at/kiwix/content/wikipedia_en_100_2023-11/A/Apollo_13"}, {"title": "www.slideshare.net", "url": "https://www.slideshare.net/slideshow/apollo-11-115193652/115193652"}, {"title": "apollo 13 saturn v", "url": "https://orbitcodex.com/operations/apollo-13-saturn-v"}, {"title": "Apollo 12", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.com/wiki/Apollo_12"}, {"title": "Apollo 12", "url": "https://he.wikipedia.org@en.wikipedia.com/wiki/Apollo_12"}]}, "Here are the launch masses from the results:\n\n- **Apollo 11:** One student slideshow gives about 45,702 kg (100,756 lb) for the launch mass. That source is weak, so I'd want to confirm it against NASA or another authoritative reference. Apollo 11 launch mass listed as 100,756 pounds (45,702 kg)\n- **Apollo 12:** Wikipedia lists about 49,915 kg. Launch mass: 49,915 kg (110,044 lb)\n- **Apollo 13:** Wikipedia gives about 44,069 kg, split between the command/service module and the lunar module. Launch mass: 44,069 kg (CSM: 28,881 kg; LM: 15,188 kg)\n\nApollo 12 is the heaviest of the three by these figures, and Apollo 13 the lightest. Apollo 13's number is the spacecraft only, and the results do not say whether it includes the Saturn V's upper stages. One result gives a separate figure for the whole Saturn V rocket at liftoff, about 2.9 million kg, but that is a different measurement. This three-stage liquid-propellant super heavy-lift launch vehicle stood 110.6 meters tall and had a lift-off mass of approximately 2.9 million kg."], "durationSeconds": 6.544936207999999, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01XojzaPGPSaZ5Py5UGS2hLD", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
