{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01KfgFq42p1ESkWsKoQVMmxC", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11\"}, {\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_Lunar_Module\"}, {\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_(spacecraft)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_command_and_service_module\"}, {\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template:Infobox_spaceflight/testcases\"}, {\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_program\"}, {\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lunar_Module_Eagle\"}, {\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space_capsule\"}, {\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/InSight\"}, {\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_12\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T12:59:47.040Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Apollo 11 wikipedia spacecraft properties launch mass kg", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01D1krNBJAi8XWqQL997hSmv", "content": [{"title": "Apollo 11", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11"}, {"title": "Apollo Lunar Module", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_Lunar_Module"}, {"title": "Apollo (spacecraft)", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_(spacecraft)"}, {"title": "Apollo command and service module", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_command_and_service_module"}, {"title": "Template:Infobox spaceflight/testcases", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template:Infobox_spaceflight/testcases"}, {"title": "Apollo program", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_program"}, {"title": "Lunar Module Eagle", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lunar_Module_Eagle"}, {"title": "Space capsule", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space_capsule"}, {"title": "InSight", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/InSight"}, {"title": "Apollo 12", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_12"}]}, "The main Apollo 11 Wikipedia article gives a launch mass of 109,646 lb (49,735 kg) for the spacecraft as a whole. That is the figure the search results most directly support.\n\nOther sources give component-level numbers that don't add up to that total:\n- A Wikipedia infobox test page lists the command module at 5,560 kg, the service module at 23,243 kg, and the lunar module at 15,095 kg. Those sum to about 43,900 kg.\n- The Apollo program article gives the combined command/service module and lunar module as 96,886 lb (43,947 kg). That matches the component sum, so the gap to 49,735 kg is probably hardware such as the spacecraft-lunar module adapter and launch escape system, which the Apollo spacecraft article gives separate masses for. That explanation is my inference, not something a source states.\n\nOther useful figures from the results:\n- The lunar module Eagle (LM-5) has a launch mass of 15,102.1 kg, per its Wikipedia article.\n- The Apollo command and service module article gives the Block II CSM as 28,800 kg fully fueled at lunar launch.\n- The Apollo 12 article gives Apollo 11's spacecraft mass as 49,735 kg, consistent with the main article."], "durationSeconds": 7.412676665999999, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01KfgFq42p1ESkWsKoQVMmxC", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
